const contents = [{"label": "What is the main difference between Markethink and a freelancer?", "id": "what-is-the-main-difference-between-markethink-and-a-freelancer"}, {"label": "Which is more consistent week to week?", "id": "which-is-more-consistent-week-to-week"}, {"label": "Who reviews the work before it goes out?", "id": "who-reviews-the-work-before-it-goes-out"}, {"label": "Which covers more channels?", "id": "which-covers-more-channels"}, {"label": "Which is faster?", "id": "which-is-faster"}, {"label": "Which costs less per month?", "id": "which-costs-less-per-month"}, {"label": "Who owns the work and the accounts?", "id": "who-owns-the-work-and-the-accounts"}, {"label": "When is a freelancer the better choice?", "id": "when-is-a-freelancer-the-better-choice"}, {"label": "FAQ", "id": "faq"}, {"label": "Try the weekly version", "id": "try-the-weekly-version"}];
const bodyHtml = "<p>Markethink is an AI marketing team for small businesses: a named AI marketing employee does the work every week, and expert marketers review it before anything goes out. Here is how that compares with hiring a freelancer, point by point.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Comparison table\" tabindex=\"0\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Freelance marketer</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">Markethink</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Best for</td>\n<td>One clear project with an end date</td>\n<td>Steady weekly marketing across channels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Consistency</td>\n<td>Depends on one person's schedule</td>\n<td>A weekly plan that keeps running</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Review before it goes out</td>\n<td>You review it</td>\n<td>Expert marketers review it, then you approve public posts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Channels covered</td>\n<td>Usually one or two specialties</td>\n<td>Social, SEO and blog, email outreach, newsletters, reports, website updates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Speed</td>\n<td>Depends on their queue</td>\n<td>Revisions in your chat, often the same day (examples below)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cost per month</td>\n<td>Varies by person and scope; no reliable public figure</td>\n<td>From $1,000/month</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Who owns the work</td>\n<td>Agree it in writing</td>\n<td>Your accounts and website stay in your name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Languages</td>\n<td>Depends on the person</td>\n<td>English and Spanish</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-the-main-difference-between-markethink-and-a-freelancer\">What is the main difference between Markethink and a freelancer?</h2>\n<p>A freelancer is one person selling their skill and time. Markethink is a team: a named AI marketing employee does the work every week, and expert marketers check it before it reaches you. With a freelancer you manage and review the work yourself; with Markethink the review is built in.</p>\n<p>Both can be good. The question is whether you need a specialist for a project, or a steady marketing rhythm that doesn't depend on one person.</p>\n<h2 id=\"which-is-more-consistent-week-to-week\">Which is more consistent week to week?</h2>\n<p>Markethink is built for consistency: your employee works from a weekly plan and doesn't take holidays, get booked by a bigger client or move on. A good freelancer can be very consistent too, but the work pauses when they are sick, busy or leave, and you start over with someone new.</p>\n<p>Consistency matters most for work that only pays off when it keeps going: social posting, follow-up emails, newsletters and SEO pages.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-reviews-the-work-before-it-goes-out\">Who reviews the work before it goes out?</h2>\n<p>With a freelancer, you are usually the reviewer. With Markethink, expert marketers review every client-facing piece against our quality bar before it reaches you, and public posts still wait for your approval. You get two checks instead of one, and you only see work that is ready.</p>\n<p>When something is off, you say so in plain words in your chat. The employee revises and remembers the correction next time. For example, Villazzo's owner reviews posts for two brands on one shared page, and nothing goes out without the owner's approval.</p>\n<h2 id=\"which-covers-more-channels\">Which covers more channels?</h2>\n<p>Markethink covers more channels with one point of contact: social media, SEO and AI search visibility, blog articles, email outreach, newsletters, presentations, reports and website updates. Most freelancers specialize in one or two of these, so covering several usually means hiring and managing several freelancers.</p>\n<p>If you only need one channel done brilliantly, a specialist freelancer may be the better fit.</p>\n<h2 id=\"which-is-faster\">Which is faster?</h2>\n<p>Markethink is usually faster on routine work and revisions, because the employee works in your chat and edits often go live the same day. Freelancers work through their own queue, so turnaround depends on how busy they are. For a complex creative project, a skilled freelancer's time can be worth the wait.</p>\n<p>Two real examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mango Media</strong>, a web agency in Niagara, Ontario, needed a 15-slide RFP proposal the same day. Its Markethink employee built it as a live web presentation and applied about 15 rounds of edits in one afternoon. The founder submitted it that day.</li>\n<li><strong>Pambuddha Homes</strong>, a South Florida custom home builder, asked for meetings on a Tuesday. Its outreach employee emailed the warm contacts the same evening, and interested replies reach the owner's chat within minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"which-costs-less-per-month\">Which costs less per month?</h2>\n<p>Markethink plans start at $1,000 per month for steady weekly work. Freelancer costs vary too widely by person, skill and scope to give one fair figure, so compare quotes for the same work over the same period, and count the time you spend briefing and reviewing a freelancer yourself.</p>\n<p>A simple way to compare: write down what needs to go out each month (for example 12 posts, 2 blog articles, 1 newsletter and weekly follow-up emails), ask a freelancer to quote it, and compare that with a Markethink plan, from $1,000 per month. Ad spend is separate in both cases.</p>\n<h2 id=\"who-owns-the-work-and-the-accounts\">Who owns the work and the accounts?</h2>\n<p>You should own your accounts, website and published work either way. Markethink works through your own accounts and the access you approve, so your posts, pages and email lists stay with you. With a freelancer, agree in writing who owns files, designs and logins before work starts.</p>\n<h2 id=\"when-is-a-freelancer-the-better-choice\">When is a freelancer the better choice?</h2>\n<p>A freelancer is the better choice when you have one project with a clear end, like a new website, a brand identity or a video; when you need deep specialist skill, like advanced paid ads or animation; or when you already have someone in-house to brief and review the work.</p>\n<p>We would rather tell you that than sell you the wrong thing. Many owners use both: a freelancer for one-off creative work, and Markethink for the weekly marketing after it. For a wider view, read <a href=\"/compare/alternatives-to-a-marketing-agency/\">alternatives to a marketing agency</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faq\">FAQ</h2>\n<details><summary>Can I use a freelancer and Markethink together?</summary><p>Yes. A common setup is a freelancer for one-off design or video work and Markethink for the weekly posts, emails and pages that follow.</p></details>\n\n<details><summary>Is Markethink a person or software?</summary><p>Both. A named AI marketing employee does the work, and expert marketers at Markethink review it before anything goes out. Our founder, Santiago Sosa, has run marketing for businesses since 2004.</p></details>\n\n<details><summary>Does Markethink work in Spanish?</summary><p>Yes. Markethink works in English and Spanish, for businesses in the United States, Canada and Latin America.</p></details>\n\n<details><summary>What if I don&#x27;t like the work?</summary><p>Say no and tell us why, in plain words. The work is revised, and the correction is remembered for next time.</p></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"try-the-weekly-version\">Try the weekly version</h2>\n<p>See what your Markethink employee would do in its first week, and decide for yourself. <a href=\"/schedule-a-walkthrough/\">Request a walkthrough</a></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>About the author:</strong> Santiago Sosa founded Markethink in 2026 in Miami. He has led All Digital Media since 2004 and was Marketing Director at a law office from 2010 to 2017. <a href=\"/authors/santiago-sosa/\">More about Santiago</a></p>";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} image="/images/hero-image.png" type="article" includeSiteEntities={true}>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(pageSchema)} />
  <Navbar />
  <main class="article-page">
    <article>
      <header class="article-hero">
        <div class="container article-hero-copy">
          <h1>Markethink vs hiring a freelance marketer</h1>
          <p class="article-meta">By Santiago Sosa, Founder · Updated 23 November 2026</p>
          <p class="article-excerpt">A freelance marketer is often the better choice for one well-defined job, like a logo, a website build or an ad campaign. Markethink fits when you need marketing done every week across several channels: a named AI marketing employee does the work, expert marketers review it, and plans start at $1,000 per month.</p>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="container article-layout">
        <aside class="article-sidebar" aria-label="In this guide">
          <nav class="sidebar-panel" aria-label="Article contents">
            <p class="sidebar-label">In this guide</p>
            <ol>{contents.map((item) => <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>)}</ol>
          </nav>
        </aside>
        <div class="article-content" set:html={bodyHtml} />
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
